IOKit's virtual member function comparisons on a compiler without Apple clang's __builtin_load_member_function_pointer
(upstream LLVM, which macOS-DroidVM builds this kernel with on Linux): there OSMemberFunctionCast of a virtual function
yields its virtual thunk, the same for every receiver, so
- IOWorkLoop::eventSourcePerformsWork compared every event source passive and no IOInterruptEventSource ever ran
  (IOMobileFramebufferLegacy's power state changes): all are active unless marked kPassive (polling a passive source does
  nothing);
- IOService::handleRegisterPowerDriver dropped every power informee whose powerStateWillChangeTo compared equal to the
  root's, overrides included: they are kept.
Under Apple clang (the iPadOS and macOS builds of this repository) both guards are false and the code is Apple's.
From macOS-DroidVM patches/xnu-12377/0015 and IOServicePM-virtual-thunk-callbacks (lateautumn233).

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOServicePM.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOServicePM.cpp
index cd18d0d..dfb7a2d 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOServicePM.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOServicePM.cpp
@@ -1261,7 +1261,6 @@ IOService::handleRegisterPowerDriver( IOPMRequest * request )
 	IOPMPowerStateIndex   numberOfStates = (IOPMPowerStateIndex) request->fArg2;
 	IOPMPowerStateIndex   i, stateIndex;
 	IOPMPowerStateIndex   lowestPowerState;
-	IOService *           root;
 	OSIterator *          iter;
 
 	PM_ASSERT_IN_GATE();
@@ -1336,7 +1335,12 @@ IOService::handleRegisterPowerDriver( IOPMRequest * request )
 		// it does nothing. One ramification of not always registering
 		// is the one fewer retain count held.
 
-		root = getPlatform()->getProvider();
+#if !__has_builtin(__builtin_load_member_function_pointer) && __has_feature(ptrauth_member_function_pointer_type_discrimination)
+		// This compiler returns the same virtual thunk for every receiver.
+		// Keep the callbacks: comparing those thunks would discard overrides.
+		{
+#else
+		IOService *root = getPlatform()->getProvider();
 		assert(root);
 		if (!root ||
 		    ((OSMemberFunctionCast(void (*)(void),
@@ -1347,6 +1351,7 @@ IOService::handleRegisterPowerDriver( IOPMRequest * request )
 		    root, &IOService::powerStateWillChangeTo)) !=
 		    ((OSMemberFunctionCast(void (*)(void),
 		    this, &IOService::powerStateWillChangeTo))))) {
+#endif
 			if (fInterestedDrivers->findItem(powerDriver) == NULL) {
 				PM_LOCK();
 				fInterestedDrivers->appendNewInformee(powerDriver);
